title: Linux: Pending updates with zero-day, critical, security and normal tiers
agents: linux
catalog: os/misc
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 Evaluates pending package updates on Debian/Ubuntu (apt), RHEL family and
 Fedora (dnf, yum) and SUSE (zypper), collected by the agent plug-in
 linux_updates (Agent Bakery rule "APT/DNF/Zypper: Linux update check (agent plug-in)").
 Nothing is installed. Every update is put into one tier: zero-day (fixes a
 CVE listed in the CISA KEV catalog), critical (high severity or EPSS above
 threshold), security or normal. Zero-day and critical can be switched off.
 Each tier has its own delay, counted from the time the agent first saw the
 package version, its own state and an optional escalation. CVEs come from
 the distribution advisories (dnf/yum/zypper) or from OSV data (apt); KEV,
 EPSS and OSV data are created by linux_updates_threatdb on the site.

discovery:
 One service is created on each host that sends the linux_updates section.
